{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790328256,"nonce":"LlAeU0urhp5beN7StWCrF0ruZ9I=","title":"LLVM closure promotion panics on bench_records: struct return where a pointer is expected","message":"With ZYNTAX_LLVM_CLOSURE_PROMOTION=1 and ZYPY_LLVM=1, crates/zyntax_python/benchmarks/bench_records.py makes the LLVM compile panic five times on beadie-promoter (llvm_backend.rs:2297, 'Found StructValue ... %\"struct.InternedString\" = type { i64, i64, i64 } but expected PointerValue'): a callee compiled into the closure returns a three-word struct by value where the caller's lowering expects its address. The panic is caught, the promotion fails, and the output is right. Same count on main (0f0e5585) and on fix/llvm-no-reopt, NUC x86_64 release. Closure promotion is off by default.","files":null}]}